{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "3f7c1b90-6c4a-4f2e-9a10-8d5b2e7c4a11",
    "name": "SatusBlockchain",
    "description": "API collection da blockchain didática SatusBlockchain.\n\nANTES DE COMECAR:\n1. Suba o no com DIFFICULTY=4.\n2. Confira a variavel node1Url (padrao http://localhost:8080).\n3. Se mudar a DIFFICULTY, atualize a variavel difficulty (ela e usada no teste de Proof of Work).\n\nORDEM: execute os requests de 1 a 8. Para rodar tudo de uma vez com os testes automatizados, use o Collection Runner (botao 'Run').",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "node1Url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "node2Url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081"
    },
    {
      "key": "node3Url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8082"
    },
    {
      "key": "difficulty",
      "value": "4"
    },
    {
      "key": "prometheusUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:9090"
    },
    {
      "key": "jaegerUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:16686"
    },
    {
      "key": "lokiUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3100"
    },
    {
      "key": "grafanaUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Situacao do no",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const no = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('identifica o no (NODE_ID)', () => pm.expect(no.node).to.be.a('string'));",
              "pm.test('existe pelo menos o genesis', () => pm.expect(no.blocks).to.be.at.least(1));",
              "pm.test('cadeia valida', () => pm.expect(no.valid).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('informa o hash do genesis (identidade da rede, etapa 10)', () => pm.expect(no.genesis).to.have.lengthOf(64));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": [""]
        },
        "description": "GET / — identidade do no, dificuldade, hash do genesis, tamanho e validade da cadeia. E o request de 'o no esta de pe?' — e, desde a etapa 10, o que o handshake de POST /peers le para conferir se um no novo nasceu do mesmo genesis."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Cadeia completa",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const cadeia = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('e uma lista de blocos', () => pm.expect(cadeia).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty);",
              "pm.test('o primeiro bloco e o genesis (indice 0)', () => pm.expect(cadeia[0].index).to.eql(0));",
              "pm.test('o genesis aponta para o hash zero', () => pm.expect(cadeia[0].previousHash).to.eql('0'));",
              "pm.test('todo bloco tem hash de 64 caracteres', () => {",
              "    cadeia.forEach((bloco) => pm.expect(bloco.hash).to.have.lengthOf(64));",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/chain",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["chain"]
        },
        "description": "GET /chain — a cadeia inteira em JSON. O bloco 0 e o genesis (mesmo em todos os nos)."
      }
    },

    {
      "name": "3. Validar cadeia",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const r = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('cadeia valida (encadeamento + PoW)', () => pm.expect(r.valid).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('informa o tamanho da cadeia', () => pm.expect(r.length).to.be.at.least(1));",
              "pm.test('informa o hash do ultimo bloco', () => pm.expect(r.latestHash).to.have.lengthOf(64));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/chain/validate",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["chain", "validate"]
        },
        "description": "GET /chain/validate — recalcula o encadeamento e o Proof of Work de toda a cadeia. Se alguem mexer num bloco, isto vira false."
      }
    },

    {
      "name": "4. Criar transacao (alice -> bob)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.test('Location aponta para a mempool', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.eql('/transactions/pending'));",
              "",
              "const tx = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('devolve a transacao recebida', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(tx.from).to.eql('alice');",
              "    pm.expect(tx.to).to.eql('bob');",
              "    pm.expect(Number(tx.amount)).to.eql(10);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"from\": \"alice\",\n  \"to\": \"bob\",\n  \"amount\": 10\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/transactions",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["transactions"]
        },
        "description": "POST /transactions — coloca a transacao na mempool (a fila de espera). Ainda NAO virou bloco: ela so entra na cadeia quando alguem minerar."
      }
    },

    {
      "name": "5. Criar transacao (bob -> carol)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "",
              "const tx = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('segunda transacao aceita na mempool', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(tx.from).to.eql('bob');",
              "    pm.expect(tx.to).to.eql('carol');",
              "    pm.expect(Number(tx.amount)).to.eql(5);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"from\": \"bob\",\n  \"to\": \"carol\",\n  \"amount\": 5\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/transactions",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["transactions"]
        },
        "description": "POST /transactions — a mempool aceita varias transacoes; todas as pendentes entram no proximo bloco minerado."
      }
    },

    {
      "name": "6. Ver pendentes (antes de minerar)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const pendentes = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('e uma lista de transacoes', () => pm.expect(pendentes).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty);",
              "pm.test('contem a transacao alice -> bob', () => {",
              "    const achou = pendentes.some((t) => t.from === 'alice' && t.to === 'bob' && Number(t.amount) === 10);",
              "    pm.expect(achou).to.be.true;",
              "});",
              "pm.test('nada foi para a cadeia ainda', () => pm.expect(pendentes.length).to.be.at.least(1));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/transactions/pending",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["transactions", "pending"]
        },
        "description": "GET /transactions/pending — o conteudo da mempool. Note que as transacoes existem aqui, mas ainda NAO estao em nenhum bloco."
      }
    },

    {
      "name": "7. Minerar bloco",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK (a cadeia nao mudou durante a mineracao)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const bloco = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('bloco encadeado no topo da cadeia', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(bloco.index).to.be.at.least(1);",
              "    pm.expect(bloco.previousHash).to.have.lengthOf(64);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Proof of Work valido (hash com N zeros)', () => {",
              "    const zeros = '0'.repeat(Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('difficulty')));",
              "    pm.expect(bloco.hash.startsWith(zeros)).to.be.true;",
              "});",
              "pm.test('leva as transacoes pendentes para dentro do bloco', () => pm.expect(bloco.transactions).to.be.an('array'));",
              "pm.test('toda transacao tem valor > 0', () => {",
              "    bloco.transactions.forEach((t) => pm.expect(Number(t.amount)).to.be.above(0));",
              "});",
              "pm.test('nonce foi encontrado (>= 0)', () => pm.expect(bloco.nonce).to.be.at.least(0));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/blocks/mine",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["blocks", "mine"]
        },
        "description": "POST /blocks/mine — minera com o que estiver na mempool e anexa o bloco a cadeia. Aqui o Proof of Work roda de verdade: na dificuldade 4 leva ~1 segundo (por isso DIFFICULTY=2 no teste manual).\n\nSe responder 409, a cadeia avancou durante a mineracao: as transacoes continuam pendentes, basta minerar de novo."
      }
    },

    {
      "name": "8. Ver pendentes (depois de minerar)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const pendentes = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('mempool esvaziada: tudo virou bloco', () => pm.expect(pendentes).to.be.an('array').that.is.empty);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/transactions/pending",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["transactions", "pending"]
        },
        "description": "GET /transactions/pending — depois da mineracao a fila fica vazia: as transacoes passaram de 'pendentes' para 'dentro do bloco 1'."
      }
    },

    {
      "name": "9. Transacao invalida (400)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
              "",
              "const erro = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('explica o motivo da recusa', () => pm.expect(erro.error).to.include('From'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"from\": \"\",\n  \"to\": \"bob\",\n  \"amount\": 10\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/transactions",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["transactions"]
        },
        "description": "POST /transactions com From vazio — a API valida a entrada e recusa com 400 (a transacao NAO entra na mempool).\n\nOutros casos que tambem dao 400: To vazio e Amount <= 0 (teste trocando o corpo)."
      }
    },

    {
      "name": "10. Cadeia depois da mineracao",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const cadeia = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('a cadeia cresceu (genesis + bloco minerado)', () => pm.expect(cadeia.length).to.be.at.least(2));",
              "pm.test('cada bloco aponta para o hash do anterior', () => {",
              "    for (let i = 1; i < cadeia.length; i++) {",
              "        pm.expect(cadeia[i].index).to.eql(cadeia[i - 1].index + 1, 'indice do bloco ' + i);",
              "        pm.expect(cadeia[i].previousHash).to.eql(cadeia[i - 1].hash, 'elo quebrado no bloco ' + i);",
              "    }",
              "});",
              "pm.test('o ultimo bloco tem as transacoes mineradas', () => {",
              "    const ultimo = cadeia[cadeia.length - 1];",
              "    pm.expect(ultimo.transactions).to.be.an('array');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/chain",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["chain"]
        },
        "description": "GET /chain — confere o encadeamento de ponta a ponta: e essa verificacao de 'previousHash de um == hash do outro' que faz a cadeia ser a cadeia."
      }
    },

    {
      "name": "11. Peers do no (etapas 6 e 10)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const r = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('identifica o no', () => pm.expect(r.node).to.be.a('string'));",
              "pm.test('peers e uma lista (vazia em no isolado)', () => pm.expect(r.peers).to.be.an('array'));",
              "pm.test('cada peer e uma URL http(s) absoluta', () => {",
              "    r.peers.forEach((peer) => pm.expect(peer.startsWith('http')).to.be.true);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/peers",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["peers"]
        },
        "description": "GET /peers — a lista ATUAL de peers do no: e para esses enderecos que o POST /blocks/mine faz push do bloco novo (POST /blocks/receive). Ela nasce de PEERS e, desde a etapa 10, muda em execucao: entra quem se anuncia (POST /peers), sai quem se despede (DELETE /peers) ou para de responder. Com os 3 containers, o node1 responde http://node2:8080 e http://node3:8080 — mais os nos criados pelo scripts/add-node.ps1; sem PEERS a lista comeca vazia. O campo url e o ADVERTISE_URL do no (null nos nos base)."
      }
    },

    {
      "name": "12. Receber transacao propagada",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 (aceita) ou 409 (ja estava na mempool: dedup)', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 409]));",
              "",
              "const r = pm.response.json();",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    pm.test('confirma que entrou na mempool local', () => pm.expect(r.accepted).to.be.true);",
              "    pm.test('informa quantas transacoes estao pendentes', () => pm.expect(r.pending).to.be.at.least(1));",
              "} else {",
              "    pm.test('a recusa vem explicada (duplicada ou ja confirmada)', () => pm.expect(r.accepted).to.be.false);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"from\": \"alice\",\n  \"to\": \"bob\",\n  \"amount\": 25\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/transactions/receive",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["transactions", "receive"]
        },
        "description": "POST /transactions/receive — o endpoint que um PEER chama (nao o cliente): e aqui que o gossip da etapa 7 entrega a transacao. 200 = entrou na mempool local; 409 = ja estava pendente (dedup) ou ja esta confirmada em um bloco."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "13. Sincronizar chain",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK (peer fora do ar e situacao normal: quem informa e o relatorio)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const relatorio = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('relatorio traz o antes/depois e o desfecho por peer', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(relatorio.previousLength).to.be.a('number');",
              "    pm.expect(relatorio.length).to.be.a('number');",
              "    pm.expect(relatorio.orphansBackToMempool).to.be.a('number');",
              "    pm.expect(relatorio.peers).to.be.an('array');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('se adotou, veio de um peer e a cadeia nao encolheu', () => {",
              "    if (relatorio.adopted !== null) {",
              "        pm.expect(relatorio.adopted.from).to.be.a('string');",
              "        pm.expect(relatorio.length).to.be.above(relatorio.previousLength);",
              "    }",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/sync",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["sync"]
        },
        "description": "POST /sync (etapa 8) — o no PUXA a cadeia de cada peer e adota a valida mais longa; as transacoes dos blocos orfaos voltam para a mempool. Troque a URL para node2Url/node3Url para recuperar um no que ficou atras. A resposta traz adopted, orphansBackToMempool e o desfecho por peer (Adopted/Kept/Invalid/Unreachable)."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "14. Metricas (GET /metrics)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK (pull: e o mesmo caminho que o Prometheus raspa)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const corpo = pm.response.text();",
              "pm.test('gauge da cadeia presente com valor numerico', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(corpo).to.match(/satus_chain_length\\{[^}]*\\} \\d+/);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('metadados TYPE do Prometheus presentes', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(corpo).to.include('# TYPE satus_chain_length gauge');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('counter de mineracao (apos o request 7) usa o sufixo _total', () => {",
              "    if (corpo.includes('satus_blocks_mined')) {",
              "        pm.expect(corpo).to.include('satus_blocks_mined_total');",
              "    }",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{node1Url}}/metrics",
          "host": ["{{node1Url}}"],
          "path": ["metrics"]
        },
        "description": "GET /metrics (etapa 9) — metricas do no no formato Prometheus, o mesmo endpoint que o Prometheus raspa. Gauges (satus_chain_length, satus_mempool_size) existem desde a subida e mostram o estado atual; counters (satus_blocks_mined_total etc.) nascem na primeira medicao. Os valores vem com labels otel_scope_name/otel_scope_version no meio (convencao do formato). Apos minerar (request 7), o valor pode levar ~2s para aparecer."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "15. Prometheus consulta metricas",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK (API HTTP do Prometheus)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const r = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('resultado e uma serie de instantaneo', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(r.status).to.eql('success');",
              "    pm.expect(r.data.resultType).to.eql('vector');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('satus_chain_length tem valor >= 1', () => {",
              "    const v = parseFloat(r.data.result[0].value[1]);",
              "    pm.expect(v).to.be.at.least(1);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('a serie identifica o no (instance)', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(r.data.result[0].metric.instance).to.be.a('string');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{prometheusUrl}}/api/v1/query?query=satus_chain_length",
          "host": ["{{prometheusUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "v1", "query"],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "query",
              "value": "satus_chain_length"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "GET /api/v1/query (Prometheus) — consulta instantanea da mesma metrica do request 14, mas pelo lado do Prometheus: prova que o PULL funcionou (ele raspa os 3 nos a cada 5s). Rode o request 7 (mine) antes e veja o valor subir em ~5s. Sem filtro, a query devolve as 3 series (um valor por no)."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "16. Prometheus targets saudaveis",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const r = pm.response.json();",
              "const alvos = r.data.activeTargets;",
              "pm.test('ao menos 4 alvos ativos: 3 nos (+ extras) + autoscraping do Prometheus', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(alvos.length).to.be.at.least(4);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('todos com health=up (scrape sem falha)', () => {",
              "    const caidos = alvos.filter(t => t.health !== 'up').map(t => t.scrapeUrl);",
              "    pm.expect(caidos).to.eql([]);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{prometheusUrl}}/api/v1/targets?state=active",
          "host": ["{{prometheusUrl}}"],
          "path": ["api", "v1", "targets"],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "state",
              "value": "active"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "GET /api/v1/targets (Prometheus) — saude de todos os alvos de scrape: os nos + o proprio Prometheus. Desde a etapa 10 os alvos sao DESCOBERTOS pelo Docker (docker_sd_configs): um node4 criado pelo scripts/add-node.ps1 aparece aqui sozinho em ate 5s, e some quando o container e removido. health=up = raspagem do /metrics funcionando; se um no cair, aparece health=down aqui (e na UI http://localhost:9090/targets)."
      }
